@startuml Buy Goods - Sequence Diagram

!define ACTOR_COLOR #FFE6E6
!define SYSTEM_COLOR #E6F3FF
!define EXTERNAL_COLOR #FFF9E6

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequence {
    ActorBackgroundColor ACTOR_COLOR
    ActorBorderColor #CC0000
    ParticipantBackgroundColor SYSTEM_COLOR
    ParticipantBorderColor #0066CC
    LifeLineBorderColor #666666
}

actor Buyer
participant "Company\nSystem" as Company
participant "IBM OS/390\nInventory" as Inventory
participant "Credit Card\nCompany" as CC
participant "Shipping\nService" as Shipping
participant "Bank" as Bank

== MAIN SUCCESS SCENARIO ==

Buyer -> Company: 1. Call with purchase request
Company -> Company: 2. Capture buyer details & goods
Company -> Inventory: 3. Check inventory (IBM OS/390)
Inventory -> Company: Inventory data retrieved
Company -> Buyer: 4. Provide goods info, prices, delivery dates
Buyer -> Company: 5. Confirm order details & sign
Company -> Company: 6. Create order in system
Company -> Shipping: 7. Ship order to buyer
Company -> Buyer: 8. Ship invoice to buyer
Buyer -> Buyer: 9. Receive goods & verify order
Buyer -> Company: 10. Pay invoice
Company -> Company: 11. Record payment

== EXTENSION 3a: OUT OF STOCK ==

note over Company, Inventory
  If inventory check (step 3) finds out-of-stock items:
  (This should rarely happen)
end note

Company -> Inventory: 3. Check inventory
Inventory -> Company: Some items out of stock
Company -> Buyer: 3a1. Inform buyer of out-of-stock items
Buyer -> Company: 3a2. Choose: wait/substitute/remove item
Company -> Company: 3a3. Return to step 4

== EXTENSION 4a: EXPEDITED SHIPPING ==

note over Company
  If buyer requests expedited shipping (step 4):
end note

Company -> Company: 4a1. Calculate expedited shipping cost
Company -> Buyer: 4a2. Provide expedited shipping quote
Buyer -> Company: 4a3. Accept or decline expedited shipping
Company -> Company: 4a4. Return to step 5

== EXTENSION 5a: DIRECT CREDIT CARD PAYMENT ==

note over Buyer, CC
  If buyer pays directly with credit card (step 5):
end note

Buyer -> Company: 5a1. Provide credit card information
Company -> CC: 5a2. Take payment by credit card (UC-044)
CC -> Company: Payment processed
Company -> Company: 5a3. Continue to step 6

== EXTENSION 7a: SHIPPING UNAVAILABLE ==

note over Company, Shipping
  If shipping service unavailable (step 7):
end note

Company -> Shipping: 7a1. Attempt to use primary shipping service
Shipping --> Company: Service unavailable
Company -> Shipping: 7a1b. Attempt backup shipping service
alt Backup available
    Shipping -> Company: Backup service available
    Company -> Shipping: Ship order via backup
else Backup unavailable
    Company -> Buyer: 7a2. Inform buyer of delay
    Company -> Shipping: 7a3. Retry when service available
    Shipping -> Company: Service available
    Company -> Shipping: Ship order
end

== EXTENSION 8a: INVOICE DELIVERY FAILS ==

note over Company, Buyer
  If invoice delivery fails (step 8):
end note

Company -> Buyer: 8a1. Retry via alternate channel (email/fax/mail)
alt All channels fail
    Company -> Company: 8a2. Log issue for manual follow-up
else Channel succeeds
    Buyer -> Buyer: Receive invoice
end

== EXTENSION 10a: BUYER RETURNS GOODS ==

note over Buyer, Company
  If buyer returns goods (step 10):
end note

Buyer -> Company: 10a1. Initiate return request
Company -> Company: 10a2. Handle returned goods (UC-105)
Company -> Buyer: 10a3. Process refund or credit

== EXTENSION 10b: BUYER DISPUTES CHARGE ==

note over Buyer, Company
  If buyer disputes charge (step 10):
end note

Buyer -> Company: 10b1. Initiate dispute resolution
Company -> Buyer: 10b2. Provide documentation
Company -> Buyer: 10b3. Resolve dispute (refund/credit/confirm)

== EXTENSION 10c: PAYMENT FAILS ==

note over Buyer, Company
  If payment fails (step 10):
end note

Company -> Bank: 10c1. Retry payment collection
Bank --> Company: Payment failed
Company -> Buyer: 10c2. Contact buyer to resolve payment issue
Buyer -> Company: Provide payment information
Company -> Bank: Retry payment
Bank -> Company: Payment received
Company -> Company: 10c3. Continue to step 11

@enduml
